Hand-written revert of 7ca76bf1 against the current tree: a Detail or EvidenceTail line that wraps a
failed attribute's Failure ("install: failed: permissions") is dropped whole again, as if it were the
Failure alone, so the caller's context in front of it is lost. unwrapFailure keeps matching the
wrapped line but returns no context for it. The pinned test fails on its "wrapped failure keeps its
context" rows by output, not by compilation.

diff --git a/internal/project/row_problem.go b/internal/project/row_problem.go
index 9db41601..7e296dde 100644
--- a/internal/project/row_problem.go
+++ b/internal/project/row_problem.go
@@ -144,8 +144,8 @@ func unwrapFailure(line string, failures []string) (context string, restated boo
 		if line == failure {
 			return "", true
 		}
-		if context, wrapped := strings.CutSuffix(line, ": "+failure); wrapped {
-			return context, true
+		if _, wrapped := strings.CutSuffix(line, ": "+failure); wrapped {
+			return "", true
 		}
 	}
 	return "", false
